  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Water and Wastewater Association Five-Year Plan 2026-2031</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Water and Wastewater Association (PWWA) will create a new five-year Strategic Plan covering 2026&#x2013;2031, replacing the current 2022&#x2013;2026 plan. The new plan will do the following: Set priorities and direction for the next five years. Improve Board governance and oversight. Give PWWA a new brand and logo along with a shared vision and goals for all members. Build on progress already made under the current plan.

PWWA will start with an organizational assessment to review current performance. It will hold a workshop with the Board and Secretariat staff to shape the plan. PWWA will include rebranding and updates to communications, IT systems, HR, and sustainability. It will  add a monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E) framework with KPIs to track progress. And it will introduce new focus areas such as Gender Equality, Disability, and Social Inclusion, which are not in the current plan.</narrative>
  </description>
